<-- Lossy stream demo

   The ~> (lossy) operator drops packets probabilistically.
   At low entropy the delivery rate is high; as entropy rises
   packets are increasingly silenced.

   This example declares a message and sends it through a lossy
   edge.  At default entropy (0) the message will almost always
   arrive.  Crank $entropy to 80+ in the header to watch it
   vanish.

   Expected output (entropy=0):
       maybe you'll see this
-->

::header::
    <o-> "lossy"
    $entropy := 0

::body::
    |msg| := "maybe you'll see this"
    |msg| ~> |print|
